["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Grouse leave small clues everywhere they live. Read them and you hunt where birds are today, not where they were last year.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 305\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Tracks drawn to scale on a 1 centimetre grid. A grouse track: 3 long toes forward and 1 short toe back, about 5 centimetres long, 75 percent. A ptarmigan track: a fuzzy print from feathered feet. A grouse walks in one zig zag line, one print in front of the next.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"305\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Tracks, to scale: 1 square = 1 cm</text>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"10\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"10\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"30\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"40\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"50\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"60\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"60\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"70\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"80\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"90\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"100\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"110\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"120\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"130\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"140\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"150\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"160\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"170\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"180\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"180\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"190\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"200\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"210\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"220\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"220\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"230\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"240\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"250\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"260\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"260\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"270\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"270\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"280\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"280\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"290\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"300\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"310\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"310\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"320\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"330\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"340\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"350\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"350\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"360\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"360\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"370\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"370\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"380\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"390\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"400\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"110\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"140\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"160\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"160\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"180\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"210\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"210\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"220\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"230\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"240\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"250\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"260\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(70 200) rotate(0)\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -50 M0 0 L-24 -40 M0 0 L24 -40 M0 0 L0 12\"/></g>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Grouse: about 5 cm</text>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3 toes forward, 1 back</text>\n<g fill=\"#9aa0a6\"><ellipse cx=\"225\" cy=\"180\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"30\"/></g>\n<text x=\"225\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ptarmigan:</text>\n<text x=\"225\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">feathered feet</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(325 245) rotate(0)\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -50 M0 0 L-24 -40 M0 0 L24 -40 M0 0 L0 12\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(345 183) rotate(0)\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -50 M0 0 L-24 -40 M0 0 L24 -40 M0 0 L0 12\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(325 121) rotate(0)\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -50 M0 0 L-24 -40 M0 0 L24 -40 M0 0 L0 12\"/></g>\n<text x=\"395\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">One line, zig zag</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Sizes 75%.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Three long toes forward, one short toe back, about 5 cm <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>One line, one print in front of the next (75 to 80%).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: tracks in detail</summary><ul><li>Forest grouse tracks are about 5 cm long: three forward toes and a short hind toe (75%, Elbroch and Marks, Bird Tracks and Sign).</li><li>In winter ruffed grouse grow comb like toe edges (pectinations), so prints look wider and fringed <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Ptarmigan feet are feathered; in snow the print can look fuzzy, with toes hard to see (Tip, 65%).</li><li>A walking grouse leaves a line of prints, one ahead of the next, gently zig zag <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Where tracks end in a spray of wing marks, the bird flew <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Hare tracks look very different: see the diagram below.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Small tracks. Snowshoe hare: two big hind prints side by side land ahead of two small front prints, making a Y that points the way it went. Grouse: 3 toes forward and 1 short toe back, about 5 to 7 cm, in a single zig zag line.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hare and grouse</text>\n  <rect x=\"15\" y=\"45\" width=\"175\" height=\"190\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#eef2f6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"210\" y=\"45\" width=\"175\" height=\"190\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#eef2f6\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#8b5a2b\">\n    <ellipse cx=\"80\" cy=\"85\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"24\"/><ellipse cx=\"125\" cy=\"85\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"24\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"102\" cy=\"140\" r=\"8\"/><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"170\" r=\"8\"/>\n  </g>\n  <path d=\"M102 225 V200\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <path d=\"M102 60 l-8 14 h16 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <text x=\"140\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">front</text>\n  <text x=\"140\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">small</text>\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">hind</text>\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"144\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">big</text>\n  <g stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\">\n    <g transform=\"translate(275 200)\"><path d=\"M0 0 V-22 M0 0 L-12 -18 M0 0 L12 -18 M0 0 V7\"/></g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(320 150)\"><path d=\"M0 0 V-22 M0 0 L-12 -18 M0 0 L12 -18 M0 0 V7\"/></g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(278 100)\"><path d=\"M0 0 V-22 M0 0 L-12 -18 M0 0 L12 -18 M0 0 V7\"/></g>\n  </g>\n  <path d=\"M355 120 l-8 14 h16 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M355 220 V134\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"260\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hare: a Y</text>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">big hind prints lead</text>\n  <text x=\"297\" y=\"260\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Grouse: 3 + 1</text>\n  <text x=\"297\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5 to 7 cm, one line</text>\n</svg>\n</figure>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 290\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Grouse droppings. Normal droppings: fibrous, about pencil thick, curved, with a white cap, about 3 centimetres long, left every day, 85 percent. Caecal droppings: soft, dark and tar like, from the ceca, green at first and dark soon after, 65 percent. A pile of droppings marks a roost or a drum log.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"290\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Grouse droppings</text>\n<path d=\"M40 120 q10 -26 30 -26\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#c4b48a\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M68 94 l4 0\" stroke=\"#ffffff\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M50 150 q14 -20 34 -20\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#b5a47a\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M82 130 l4 0\" stroke=\"#ffffff\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<line x1=\"40\" y1=\"178\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"178\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3 cm</text>\n<text x=\"110\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Fibrous, pencil thick,</text>\n<text x=\"110\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">curved, white cap.</text>\n<text x=\"110\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Daily, everywhere (85%).</text>\n<path d=\"M50 240 q10 -14 26 -6 q14 8 2 16 q-16 8 -28 -10\" fill=\"#3d2f22\"/>\n<text x=\"110\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Soft, dark, tar like:</text>\n<text x=\"110\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">from the ceca. Green</text>\n<text x=\"110\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">at first, dark fast (65%).</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(330 150)\"><path d=\"M-20 0 q4 -8 10 -8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#c4b48a\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-6 4 q4 -8 10 -8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#c4b48a\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M8 -2 q4 -8 10 -8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#c4b48a\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-14 14 q4 -8 10 -8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#c4b48a\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M2 16 q4 -8 10 -8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#c4b48a\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M14 10 q4 -8 10 -8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#c4b48a\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-4 -10 q4 -8 10 -8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#c4b48a\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></g>\n<text x=\"330\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A pile =</text>\n<text x=\"330\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">a roost or</text>\n<text x=\"330\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">drum log</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Fibrous, curved, pencil thick, white tipped <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>A pile means a roost or a drum log (75 to 85%).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what droppings tell you</summary><ul><li>Normal droppings: long curved cylinders about pencil thick, fibrous and pale tan, with white uric acid (85%, Hinterland Who's Who). Often 2.5 to 4 cm long (70%, Northern Woodlands).</li><li>Caecal droppings: soft, dark, tar like, from the ceca, passed less often (70%, Elbroch and Marks via Laura Erickson).</li><li>Fresh caecal droppings are green and turn black quickly in the sun; they break down in days to weeks (65%, Wyoming Game and Fish, sage grouse).</li><li>Pile under a tree: night roost <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Pile on one spot of a log: drum stand <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>What is in them: needles mean conifer feeding, berry seeds mean a berry patch (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Top view of a dust bowl beside a road: a shallow oval scrape in dry dirt with a few small brown feathers around it. Size around 20 to 30 centimetres across is an estimate, Tip.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A dust bowl on a road edge</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"260\" fill=\"#d9c9a6\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#c4b48a\"/>\n<text x=\"390\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Road</text>\n<ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"200\" rx=\"70\" ry=\"38\" fill=\"#b9a57e\" stroke=\"#8c7a55\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"200\" rx=\"42\" ry=\"20\" fill=\"#a8946c\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(150 170) rotate(20)\"><path d=\"M0 0 q6 -14 0 -26 q-6 12 0 26\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"-26\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(250 235) rotate(-30)\"><path d=\"M0 0 q6 -14 0 -26 q-6 12 0 26\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"-26\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(280 185) rotate(60)\"><path d=\"M0 0 q6 -14 0 -26 q-6 12 0 26\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"-26\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/></g>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Shallow scrape in dry dirt, 20 to 30 cm across,</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">a few small feathers (Tip, size my estimate).</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Shallow scrapes in dry dirt, a few feathers <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Clipped clover and dropped berries on an edge at dawn (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more sign</summary><ul><li>Dust bowls sit in dry, loose dirt on road edges, banks and root holes <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Single small body feathers near a bowl or under a roost tree are normal moult or preening (Tip).</li><li>A burst of feathers with no bird: a hawk or owl kill (Tip). Goshawks and great horned owls take adult ruffed grouse <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Feeding sign: clover leaves clipped short, kinnikinnick or rose hips missing from a patch, aspen buds snipped in winter (Tip).</li><li>Bits knocked from trees onto snow show birds feeding overhead (75%, Canadian Wildlife Federation).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation. A grouse flies down and dives into soft snow, leaving an entry hole. It tunnels a short way and spends the night under the snow. In the morning it bursts out, leaving a second hole with wing marks on both sides, then flies off. A hole plus wing marks means the bird has left.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Snow roost: dive in, burst out</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"180\" width=\"400\" height=\"120\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"180\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#b9c6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path id=\"mgr-snow-dive-p\" d=\"M40 60 Q100 120 120 185\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"16,-20 20,-28 25,-20\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g><animateMotion dur=\"2s\" fill=\"freeze\"><mpath href=\"#mgr-snow-dive-p\"/></animateMotion><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"2s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n<path d=\"M120 190 Q170 215 230 210\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#b9c6d3\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-dasharray=\"300\" stroke-dashoffset=\"300\"><animate attributeName=\"stroke-dashoffset\" from=\"300\" to=\"0\" begin=\"2s\" dur=\"1.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></path>\n<circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"182\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#b9c6d3\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"3.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Night under the snow</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><ellipse cx=\"240\" cy=\"182\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#b9c6d3\"/><path d=\"M200 180 q-20.0 -8 -40 -2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#9fb0c2\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M212 180 q-14.0 -8 -28 -2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#9fb0c2\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M268 180 q14.0 -8 28 -2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#9fb0c2\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M280 180 q20.0 -8 40 -2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#9fb0c2\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g>\n<path id=\"mgr-snow-dive-q\" d=\"M240 180 Q300 120 380 70\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5s\"/><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"16,-20 20,-28 25,-20\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g><animateMotion dur=\"1.5s\" begin=\"5s\" fill=\"freeze\"><mpath href=\"#mgr-snow-dive-q\"/></animateMotion></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"6.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"44\" width=\"260\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Hole plus wing marks = left</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Dive in at dusk, burst out at dawn. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-grouse-snow-roost.jpg\" alt=\"Roost hole with wing marks.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Roost hole with wing marks. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Cephas, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bonasa_umbellus_snow_hole.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-grouse-wing-prints.jpg\" alt=\"Wing prints where a grouse took off.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Wing prints where a grouse took off. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: John Good, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grouse_wing_prints_in_snow.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><ul><li>Hole, short tunnel, second hole with wing marks (75 to 80%).</li></ul><ul><li>Wing marks on both sides: the bird has left <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: reading a roost</summary><ul><li>Grouse fly straight into soft snow, so there may be no tracks leading in <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Inside: a small chamber, often with a pile of droppings from the night <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Exit hole with wing prints on the snow beside it: the bird burst out <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>An entry hole with no exit: the bird may still be inside. Be ready (Tip, 60%).</li><li>Snow roost sign needs soft snow about 20 cm or deeper (70 to 75%).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 305\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A ruffed grouse drum log: a big mossy log at a forest edge with an open forest floor around it so the male can see, thick cover overhead to hide from hawks, and a pile of droppings on the one spot where he stands to drum, 85 percent.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"305\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A drum log: what to look for</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<polygon points=\"60,112 6.0,232 114.0,232\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"57\" y=\"232\" width=\"6\" height=\"18\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n<polygon points=\"350,122 300.5,232 399.5,232\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"347\" y=\"232\" width=\"6\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n<rect x=\"107\" y=\"192\" width=\"6\" height=\"42\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><ellipse cx=\"110\" cy=\"174\" rx=\"27\" ry=\"31\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<rect x=\"297\" y=\"196\" width=\"6\" height=\"38\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><ellipse cx=\"300\" cy=\"180\" rx=\"24\" ry=\"28\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<rect x=\"120\" y=\"205\" width=\"170\" height=\"28\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M130 205 q30 -6 60 0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"5\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(240 200)\"><path d=\"M-12 0 q3 -6 8 -6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8e0c8\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-2 3 q3 -6 8 -6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8e0c8\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M8 -1 q3 -6 8 -6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8e0c8\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-6 -6 q3 -6 8 -6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8e0c8\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M4 -8 q3 -6 8 -6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8e0c8\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></g>\n<circle cx=\"240\" cy=\"196\" r=\"22\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<text x=\"150\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Thick cover overhead</text>\n<text x=\"150\" y=\"88\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">for hiding from hawks</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Big mossy log, open floor around it,</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">a pile of droppings on one spot (85%).</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Big mossy log, open floor, cover overhead, droppings on one spot <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>A spring drum log means a male lives here year round <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: using drum logs</summary><ul><li>The drum stand is often a big moss covered log at a forest edge <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. Stumps, boulders and mounds are used too <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>A Minnesota study recorded at least 593 logs used by drumming males <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>The male holds that territory for life <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. Find his log in April, hunt that patch in October (Tip).</li><li>Do not disturb drumming birds in spring: no season then, and it is the breeding time (99% no season; respect Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Sign</th><th>Fresh</th><th>Old</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Track in snow</td><td>Sharp edges, toe detail</td><td>Rounded, melted</td></tr><tr><td>Normal dropping</td><td>Moist, shiny white tip</td><td>Dry, faded</td></tr><tr><td>Caecal dropping</td><td>Green</td><td>Black, crusted</td></tr><tr><td>Roost hole</td><td>Crisp, no new snow</td><td>Filled, soft</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Tip: new snow overnight resets the clock. Any track on top is from today.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: detail</summary><ul><li>Track ageing is general tracking practice (Tip, 60 to 70%).</li><li>Caecal droppings green to black quickly <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Wind and sun round track edges within hours on a warm day (Tip).</li><li>Write the time and weather in your Journal next to each find (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation in snow. A fresh line of grouse tracks winds toward a conifer. You walk beside the line slowly and stop often. As you near the cover, the grouse flushes from beside the tree. Be ready near cover.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Follow a fresh track line</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"260\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n<path id=\"mgr-track-follow-p\" d=\"M20 270 Q120 240 160 200 Q210 150 280 140\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(40 265) rotate(60)\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -12 M0 0 L-6 -10 M0 0 L6 -10\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(70 258) rotate(60)\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -12 M0 0 L-6 -10 M0 0 L6 -10\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(100 248) rotate(60)\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -12 M0 0 L-6 -10 M0 0 L6 -10\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(128 232) rotate(60)\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -12 M0 0 L-6 -10 M0 0 L6 -10\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(152 212) rotate(60)\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -12 M0 0 L-6 -10 M0 0 L6 -10\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(176 188) rotate(60)\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -12 M0 0 L-6 -10 M0 0 L6 -10\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(205 166) rotate(60)\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -12 M0 0 L-6 -10 M0 0 L6 -10\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(235 152) rotate(60)\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -12 M0 0 L-6 -10 M0 0 L6 -10\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(262 144) rotate(60)\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -12 M0 0 L-6 -10 M0 0 L6 -10\"/></g>\n<polygon points=\"320,80 284.0,160 356.0,160\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"317\" y=\"160\" width=\"6\" height=\"12\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n<g><circle r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><animateMotion dur=\"6s\" fill=\"freeze\" keyPoints=\"0;0.8\" keyTimes=\"0;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"><mpath href=\"#mgr-track-follow-p\"/></animateMotion></g>\n<path id=\"mgr-track-follow-q\" d=\"M300 150 Q340 90 395 60\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5.5s\"/><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.55 0.55)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"16,-20 20,-28 25,-20\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g><animateMotion dur=\"1.2s\" begin=\"5.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"><mpath href=\"#mgr-track-follow-q\"/></animateMotion></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"1s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Slow down. Stop often.</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"76\" width=\"240\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"97\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Flush near cover: be ready</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Slow down near cover. The bird is close. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Walk beside the line, not on it (Tip).</li><li>Slow down as tracks near cover (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: following a grouse track line</summary><ul><li>Fresh tracks in new snow mean the bird is close, often within 50 m (Tip).</li><li>Walk beside the tracks so you can read them again if you lose the line (Tip).</li><li>Tracks wander and stop under a conifer: look up (Tip).</li><li>Tracks end in a burst of wing marks: it flew. Look ahead for the next tree it may sit in (Tip).</li><li>Gun ready, finger off the trigger, safety on until you shoulder (Tip; safety habit).</li><li>See also <a href=\"#/s/tracks\">Tracks</a> and <a href=\"#/s/snow-tracking\">Snow tracking</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 305\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Tracks drawn to scale on a 1 centimetre grid. A grouse track: 3 long toes forward and 1 short toe back, about 5 centimetres long, 75 percent. A ptarmigan track: a fuzzy print from feathered feet. A grouse walks in one zig zag line, one print in front of the next.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"305\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Tracks, to scale: 1 square = 1 cm</text>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"10\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"10\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"30\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"40\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"50\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"60\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"60\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"70\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"80\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"90\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"100\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"110\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"120\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"130\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"140\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"150\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"150\"