\"230\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"240\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"250\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"260\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(70 200) rotate(0)\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -50 M0 0 L-24 -40 M0 0 L24 -40 M0 0 L0 12\"/></g>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Grouse: about 5 cm</text>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3 toes forward, 1 back</text>\n<g fill=\"#9aa0a6\"><ellipse cx=\"225\" cy=\"180\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"30\"/></g>\n<text x=\"225\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ptarmigan:</text>\n<text x=\"225\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">feathered feet</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(325 245) rotate(0)\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -50 M0 0 L-24 -40 M0 0 L24 -40 M0 0 L0 12\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(345 183) rotate(0)\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -50 M0 0 L-24 -40 M0 0 L24 -40 M0 0 L0 12\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(325 121) rotate(0)\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -50 M0 0 L-24 -40 M0 0 L24 -40 M0 0 L0 12\"/></g>\n<text x=\"395\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">One line, zig zag</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Sizes 75%.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Rhyme: \"Three toes ahead and one behind, a grouse's line is what you'll find.\"</li><li>Number trick: \"5 cm and 50 m\": track length, and how close the bird often is.</li><li>Old hand's rule (tradition): \"Fresh track, slow feet.\"</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li>\"Pile on a log, drummer in the bog.\"</li><li>\"Hole and wings, the bird has gone; hole alone, the bird sits on.\"</li><li>\"Green goo new, black goo old.\"</li><li>Hooks are made for this course; slowing down on a fresh track is widely repeated advice.</li></ul></details>","<ul><li>Hinterland Who's Who, Elbroch and Marks (Bird Tracks and Sign), Northern Woodlands. Checked 2026-10-11.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.hww.ca/en/wildlife/birds/ruffed-grouse.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hinterland Who's Who, Ruffed grouse</a>, read directly <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Elbroch and Marks, Bird Tracks and Sign (Stackpole), via earlier app research and <a href=\"https://blog.lauraerickson.com/2018/02/get-grip.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Laura Erickson's summary</a>, search preview (70 to 80%).</li><li><a href=\"https://northernwoodlands.org/articles/article/tracking-tips-ruffed-grouse\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Northern Woodlands, Tracking tips: ruffed grouse</a>, search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://wgfd.wyo.gov/Ask-Game-and-Fish/span-id-docs-internal-guid-a28e6712-7fff-283f-09ee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wyoming Game and Fish, caecal droppings (sage grouse)</a>, search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Drumming log study, Cloquet Forest, The Auk 84, search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Snow roosts: Wilson Bulletin; Heinrich; Idaho Fish and Game (70 to 75%).</li><li>Canadian Wildlife Federation ruffed grouse page, search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>All checked 2026-10-11. Full log: <code>research/2026-10-11-masterclass-grouse.md</code>.</li></ul></details>"]